.TH "lfe_cl" "3" "2017" ""
.SH NAME
cl \- LFE Common Lisp interface library
.SH SYNOPSIS
This module provides a set of Common Lisp functions and macros for use
in LFE.
The definitions closely follow the CL definitions and won\(cqt be
documented here.
.SH DATA TYPES
The boolean values used here are the standard LFE \f[CR]true\f[R] and
\f[CR]false\f[R] and \f[B]NOT\f[R] the Common Lisp values.
.SH EXPORTS
.SS Boolean conversion functions
\f[B]\f[CB](make\-lfe\-bool cl\-value)\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB](make\-cl\-bool lfe\-bool)\f[B]\f[R]
.SS Control structures
\f[B]\f[CB](do vars (end\-test result) body)                          [macro]\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
The value of \f[CR]body\f[R] is bound the variable \f[CR]do\-state\f[R]
which can be used when updating vars and in the \f[CR]end\-test\f[R].
This is the only way to get a value out of the body.
